  "explainer": {
    "summary": "Rockstar's Grand Theft Auto VI launched on November 19, 2026, on PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X/S, and this weekend is its first on sale.",
    "why_now": "This is launch week. Sony said on November 10 it had become the most pre-ordered game in PlayStation Store history, and digital pre-loads of up to 212 GB opened nine days before release.",
    "background": [
      "Sony's record covers the PlayStation Store only, not every platform. Physical copies went on sale from November 12 with a download code in the box rather than a full game on disc. Sales figures circulating since launch come from mixed sources, some third-party estimates, and conflicting launch-day numbers have appeared, so treat any single figure with care.",
      "The feeds also show GTA V Enhanced and GTA V Legacy high on Steam's charts. Those are the older game on PC; GTA VI's release covers consoles only."
    ],
